msgid "Connecting with Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-bluetooth-connectivity.rst:55
#: 1497590857e94d5f9d5044b7a4271e25
msgid "Many PCs and Laptops have bluetooth adapters built in but if not then you can use a generic USB Bluetooth dongle (pic above) or use an additional Bluetooth data link connected via an `FTDI Cable <https://www.amazon.com/ftdi-adapter/s?k=ftdi+adapter>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-bluetooth-connectivity.rst:60
#: a1a91289aa1a4af5833ebfca3e8c1505
msgid "After first making sure your autopilot is powered on, and your PC's bluetooth dongle is plugged in and installed, click on the Windows task bar's little up triangle (aka \"show hidden icons\") which should be on the bottom right of the screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-bluetooth-connectivity.rst:68
#: a3be6ecb9e2b49da9f6471961f7e171e
msgid "The \"hidden icons box\" should appear. Right-mouse-button-click on the BlueTooth icon and select \"show Bluetooth devices\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-bluetooth-connectivity.rst:77
#: 204c82c58d694ebcb308078b4f313f2c
msgid "Windows should bring up the devices box. Any devices you may already have connected by Bluetooth will be in this box. If you have not connected any BT devices before this box will be empty. Select \"Add a device\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-mission-planner-bluetooth-connectivity.rst:85
#: 2dfb5c5b289d41adb6b9936a399ea659
msgid "Windows will search for BT devices for you. If you have any BT devices turned on they will show up here (like perhaps your cell phone) ignore any other devices and select the HC-05 or HC-06 (or Linvor) ."
msgstr ""

